  <release>0.5.0</release>
  <api>0.5.0</api>
 </version>
 <stability>
  <release>alpha</release>
  <api>alpha</api>
 </stability>
 <license uri="https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT">MIT</license>
 <notes>0.5.0: Scope::__run_without(), not part of the RFC, lets an event loop running in a scope of its own keep that scope out of the state switching. Scope switches are cheaper (the superglobals are moved without being compared, and the per-fiber bookkeeping and a missing $_SESSION cost no lookups). Fixes: a crash in C code reading the request arrays after a scope made a superglobal a reference or a non-array; a new scope dropping a save handler module another extension had put in place of ext/session's; a superglobal deleted from the end of the symbol table being confused with the variable added after it.</notes>
